<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Puducherry (union territory)</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Pondicherry (union territory)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Puducherry is a union territory of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> formed from the four former French settlements of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pondicherry">Pondicherry</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karaikal">Karaikal</a>, Mahé and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yanam">Yanam</a>, which lie hundreds of kilometres apart. They were transferred to India de facto in 1954 and legally in 1962, and became a union territory in 1963. Its capital is the city of Puducherry, and French retains official status alongside Tamil, Malayalam, Telugu and English.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/puducherry-union-territory.jpg" alt="Puducherry (union territory)" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Karthik Easvur · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pondicherry-Rock_beach_aerial_view.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
